<title>UK: RTZ up on firm copper price, CRA rise.</title>
<headline>RTZ up on firm copper price, CRA rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in RTZ Corp Plc rose on Thursday, against the trend of a declining overall market, after recent strength in copper prices and gains in shares in its CRA unit in Australia, traders said.</p>
<p>RTZ was up 13-1/2p at 955-1/2 by 1005 GMT while CRA was up 19 Australian cents at A$20.00.  </p>
<p>Copper reached a five-month high on Wednesday around $2,240 a tonne. &quot;We have had a move in copper and a move in CRA and that has helped,&quot; said one market-maker in RTZ shares</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
